# Act 3, chapter 8 "The Massacre" (Age 767, West City, world 17). Flags: 340 opened, 341 the stall memory, 342 the
# Z Fighters land, 343 Vegeta, 344 the mother and son spared, 345 Tien, 346 Yamcha, 347 Krillin, 348 Piccolo,
# 349 chapter end (345/346 are set by the Tien/Yamcha scenes), 350 Vegeta's last words seen, 351 Krillin aftermath seen. Boss deaths (log4/stats.json death
# scripts) set their flag and load the next area; each area's arrival trigger plays the next scene.
# Speakers: #144/#145 Vegeta, #112 Piccolo, #90 Krillin, #135 Tien, #159 Yamcha (BF portraits), gohan_teen (LoG2).
list ch8_start
set_flag 340
do call 183 516 1464 1465
do call 115 0 2 0 0 0; call 121 1
do call 120 1; call 119 17 1 1 268 304; call 121 60
narrate Age 767. West City, three days later.
say android18 This is it. This is where we used to live.
say android17 Huh. It's smaller than I remember.
say android18 Everything is.
say android17 Come on. I want a new jacket. Mine smells like Gero's lab.
narrate Seventeen walks into Z-Mart and back out with a jacket nobody sold him. Nobody stops him. Nobody even looks up.
say android17 See? Easy. Nobody chases us anymore.
say android18 We used to run from that store. The man behind the counter had a broom. Do you remember?
say android17 ...No.
say android18 Our old hideout was down by the docks. The warehouse. I want to see it.
say android17 Sentimental. Fine. But if it's boring, we're leaving.
journal Visit the old hideout at the docks
do call 47; call 51 0
# ---------- the fruit stall (Hercule's old spot): the first memory
list ch8_stall
if_flag 341 stall_again
unless_flag 359 stall_early
set_flag 341
narrate A woman sells fruit from a cart. Her daughter, maybe eight, sorts the apples by colour and hums to herself.
narrate Fruit seller: Would you like an apple, miss? On the house. You look tired.
say android18 I don't get tired.
narrate The girl holds one out with both hands. She has a little backpack on, the straps let out too long for her.
narrate Rain on a bus shelter roof. A girl with a backpack too big for her, breaking a stolen apple in half.
narrate "Half for you, half for me, Lapis. That's the rule."
say android17 Eighteen? You're making a face.
say android18 Did we ever split things? Food. When we were small.
say android17 How should I know? That was somebody else.
narrate Eighteen takes the apple. She doesn't eat it.
narrate Then the birds stop singing. All of them, all at once.
say android17 Feel that? Five... no, six of them. Big power. Coming fast.
say android18 Coming here.
say android17 Finally, something interesting. The big crossroads. Let's give them an audience.
journal Meet them at the crossroads
do call 47; call 51 0
stop
label stall_again
narrate Fruit seller: Take care of yourself, miss. Whatever it is, it'll look better tomorrow.
stop
label stall_early
narrate Fruit seller: Fresh apples! Pears! ...Oh, are you two just looking? Come back any time.
say android18 Later. The docks first.
# ---------- townsfolk
list ch8_man
narrate Man: Did you hear? Goku's dead. Not a monster, not a war. A heart virus. The man who saved the world twice, and a sickness got him.
narrate Man: Makes you think, doesn't it? Nobody's looking out for us now.
list ch8_woman
narrate Woman: Lovely morning. Are you two new in town? You look like you could use a hot meal. There's a place by the park.
say android18 We know the place.
list ch8_police
narrate Police officer: Move along, kids. ...Hey. Don't I know you two? There were a pair of runaways, years back. Lapis and...
narrate Police officer: No. Those kids would be grown up by now. Forget it.
# ---------- the crossroads: the Z Fighters land (17:1 trigger -> 17:2)
list ch8_landing
unless_flag 341 not_yet
set_flag 342
do call 149 1
narrate The wind changes. Six figures drop out of a clear sky and land in the middle of the street.
do call 120 20; call 119 17 2 1 424 464; call 121 20
say #112 Red Ribbon markings. So the old rumours were true. Dr. Gero's work.
say #90 They're... kids. They look like normal kids, Piccolo.
say #112 They are not. Look at their eyes, Krillin.
say gohan_teen Mr. Piccolo... Dad was supposed to be here for this. He always knew what to do.
say #112 Your father isn't here, Gohan. We are.
say android17 You're the ones who used to follow Goku around. The heroes.
say #144 Heroes? Don't lump me in with these fools.
say #144 Kakarot died in his bed, of a disease. He never gave me my rematch. I won't be cheated a second time by a pair of toasters.
say #112 Vegeta, we fight together or we don't fight at all.
say #145 I fight ALONE. Stay out of my way. All of you.
say android17 I like him. Eighteen, mind if I take this one?
say android18 Be my guest.
narrate The others pull back to the rooftops. Vegeta doesn't look at them.
do heal; call 120 20; call 119 17 3 1 424 440; call 121 20
journal Defeat Vegeta
do call 47; call 51 0
stop
label not_yet
# ---------- after Vegeta (17:4 arrival)
list ch8_after_vegeta
if_flag 350 vegeta_seen
set_flag 350
narrate Vegeta goes down on one knee. He tries to stand twice.
say #145 Kakarot... you coward. You didn't even... let me...
say android17 Was he your friend? This Goku.
say #144 ...He was my goal.
narrate He doesn't try a third time.
say #90 Vegeta! ...He's gone. Piccolo, he's really gone.
say #112 Gohan. Stay behind me.
say #159 Everybody clear the street! Shelters, now! Go, go, GO!
narrate People run. At the end of the street a bus sits with its doors jammed, faces pressed to the windows.
say #135 Yamcha, get those people out. I'll keep these two busy.
say #159 Tien, you can't take them alone!
say #135 I don't intend to win. I intend to buy you time.
journal Tien is waiting at the crossroads
do call 47; call 51 0
stop
label vegeta_seen
list ch8_civilians
if_flag 344 civ_again
set_flag 344
narrate A woman holds her son behind her. He's crying too hard to make a sound.
narrate Woman: Please. Please, he's only six.
say android17 Eighteen, they're right there. Don't tell me you're going soft.
say android18 ...Leave them.
say android17 Why?
say android18 Because I said so. They're not worth the energy.
narrate The woman doesn't wait to be told twice. Eighteen watches until she can't see them any more.
stop
label civ_again
narrate The woman can't move. She just holds on to her son and shakes.
# ---------- Tien's last stand (17:4 trigger), then Yamcha (17:6 arrival). Their BF sprites have no fighting
# animations (idle/walk only), so their deaths are scenes, not fights.
list ch8_tien
set_flag 345
say #135 I've fought a demon king. A Saiyan prince. You two don't even look like you're trying.
say android17 We're not.
say #135 Then I'll make you try.
narrate Tien puts his hands together in a triangle.
do call 120 4; call 121 4; call 120 4; call 121 4
narrate The street caves in under them. Again. And again.
do call 120 4; call 121 4; call 120 4; call 121 4
narrate Every blast takes something out of him. He keeps firing anyway.
say android17 You're going to kill yourself doing that.
say #135 Yes.
narrate Somewhere behind him, the bus engine finally turns over.
narrate Tien's hands drop. He falls forward, still facing them.
do call 120 40; call 119 17 6 1 424 440; call 121 40
list ch8_yamcha
set_flag 346
say #159 Tien... you stubborn idiot.
say #159 The bus got out. Thirty-one people. You hear me, Tien? Thirty-one.
say android18 You knew you'd lose. Both of you knew.
say #159 Yeah. Goku would have done the same thing. He'd have done it better, but... same thing.
say #159 Come on, then! I've been the weakest guy in the room my whole life. I'm used to it!
narrate Yamcha charges. He's fast, for a human. It isn't enough.
narrate Seventeen meets him halfway.
narrate Yamcha is still smiling when he goes down.
do call 120 30
do call 149 3; heal; call 119 17 7 1 424 440; call 121 30
# ---------- Krillin (arena 17:7 arrival), fought as Eighteen
list ch8_krillin
say #90 Yamcha... Tien... Vegeta...
if_flag 344 kri_spared
say #90 You. You hesitated back there, when that woman and her kid were in the street. I saw your face.
goto kri_next
label kri_spared
say #90 You. You're the one who let that woman and her kid go. I saw.
label kri_next
say android18 You saw wrong.
say #90 Maybe. I have to fight you, I know. But I don't think you want this.
say android18 Stop talking.
say #90 Okay. ...Okay.
journal Defeat Krillin
do call 47; call 51 0
# ---------- after Krillin (17:8 arrival)
list ch8_after_krillin
if_flag 351 krillin_seen
set_flag 351
narrate Krillin hits the ground and doesn't get up.
narrate Not once did he throw a punch at her face. Eighteen noticed. She can't stop noticing.
do call 136 150
say android18 ...Why didn't he hit me?
say android17 Who cares? He was weak.
say android18 He wasn't weak. He was holding back.
say android17 Then he was stupid. Same thing.
narrate Across the street, someone has watched all of it.
say #112 Gohan. When I tell you to run, you run. Don't argue with me.
say gohan_teen I'm not leaving you, Mr. Piccolo!
say #112 You're the only one who can beat them someday. Not today. Someday.
say android17 Touching. My turn.
do call 149 1
do heal; call 120 20; call 119 17 9 1 424 440; call 121 20
journal Defeat Piccolo
do call 47; call 51 0
stop
label krillin_seen
# ---------- Piccolo (arena 17:9 arrival), fought as Seventeen
list ch8_piccolo
say #112 Look at you. You think you're free. You're doing exactly what a dead man built you to do.
say android17 Shut up.
say #112 Gero wanted the world afraid of his machines. Congratulations. You're his best work.
say android17 I said SHUT UP!
do call 47; call 51 0
# ---------- Gohan runs (17:10 arrival), then the night
list ch8_run
set_flag 349
narrate Piccolo's legs give out. He's still looking at the boy.
say #112 Gohan... RUN!
do begin_moves; move gohan_bf 420 160; wait_moves
say android18 He's getting away.
say android17 Let him. It's more fun if somebody's left.
narrate Eighteen watches the small figure until it's gone. She doesn't say anything.
do call 120 60
do call 119 16 2 1 268 304; call 121 60
narrate That night. The roof of the Z-Mart.
narrate Fires burn in four places across West City. Sirens, far away.
say android17 The prince. The three-eyed one. The one with the scars. The little bald one. The green one. Five.
say android18 Lapis.
say android17 Don't call me that.
say android18 What was our mother's name?
narrate A long silence.
say android17 ...I don't know. Does it matter?
say android18 I don't know either. I've been trying all night. I can remember the broom in the shop. I can remember the rain. I can't remember her face.
say android17 Then she wasn't worth remembering.
say android18 That's not what scares me.
if_flag 344 night_spared
goto night_radio
label night_spared
say android18 That woman this morning, with the little boy. I let them go, and I don't know why.
say android17 Because you were bored.
say android18 ...Yeah. Because I was bored.
label night_radio
narrate Below them, a radio in a broken window is still on. The same words, over and over:
narrate Radio: ...two of them. Teenagers. If you see them, do not approach. Repeat, do not approach...
journal Seventeen and Eighteen
narrate End of Chapter 8.
run ch9_start
# ---------- the old hideout (areas from log4/gen_ch8.py; flags 359 tin box, 369 / 382 caches)
list ch8_hideout
if_flag 359 hideout_done
set_flag 359
narrate The old warehouse. The mattresses are long gone. Someone has painted over the red fang on the wall.
narrate Eighteen kneels by the crates and pries up a loose board without thinking about it. Her hands know where it is.
narrate A tin box. Inside: a handful of old zeni, a capsule case with a Red Ribbon mark inside the lid...
narrate ...and a strip of photo-booth pictures. Two kids pulling faces. A boy with black hair. A girl with a backpack too big for her.
say android17 Who are they?
say android18 ...Nobody.
narrate She puts the photo strip in her pocket anyway.
unless_flag 467 hideout_noruby
narrate Under the photos, wrapped in an old sock: a red stone the size of a hen's egg.
say android17 Whoa. Where did that come from?
say android18 ...For later. Somebody said that once. Put one thing away for later, for when you need it.
say android17 Need it for what? We can take anything we want now.
say android18 I know.
narrate She keeps it anyway.
do call 129 28 1
narrate Got the Ribbon Ruby.
label hideout_noruby
say android17 Hey. I know that case. I swiped it off some guy at a bus stop... didn't I?
say android18 You did. And I told you to ditch it, Lapis.
say android17 What did you just call me?
say android18 ...Seventeen. I said Seventeen.
say android18 Let's go back to the city. I want an apple.
journal Head back into West City
stop
label hideout_done
narrate The loose board. The box is empty now.
list ch8_cache_river
if_flag 382 c8river_empty
set_flag 382
narrate The rowboat has rotted through. Wedged under the seat: a sealed can of cherry soda, still cold somehow.
do call 129 4 1
stop
label c8river_empty
narrate A rotted rowboat.
list ch8_cache_docks
if_flag 369 c8docks_empty
set_flag 369
narrate The dome house is boarded up. Seventeen kicks the door in. A dusty first-aid box: an elixir and a Senzu Bean.
do call 129 7 1; call 129 11 1
stop
label c8docks_empty
narrate Nothing left in the dome house.
# ---------- Gero's note 6 (log4/gen_more.py: the Old Warehouse 17:36; flag 525)
list note_warehouse
if_flag 525 nware_read
set_flag 525
narrate Pinned behind a crate, yellow with age: a notebook page in small, careful handwriting.
narrate "Age 762. Paid a street gang to take their hideout, to see what they would do. They took it back in a day."
narrate "I was proud of them. Is that the word? I have not used it in years."
say android18 Proud. He was proud of us.
say android17 He was proud of his experiment. Don't mix those up.
do call 129 31 1
run notes_check
stop
label nware_read
narrate The crate where the page was pinned.
